Sval: launch macOS child processes by their real path

On macOS, Gecko launches each child from the GRE directory as the parent
saw it, so Sval started through a path with a symlink in it (mktemp's
/var/folders, /tmp, or a user's own link) starts its children through the
link too. A sandboxed child resolves the paths it derives from its own
executable, and the kernel needs file-read-metadata on each symlink a path
passes through. SandboxPolicyUtility grants none, so a utility process
never connects: no audio decodes, and a page whose video has an audio
track never fires load. The content, RDD, GPU and socket policies allow
file-read-metadata on "/"; the utility and GMP policies do not.
Resolving the GRE directory with realpath (nsIFile::Normalize, as
nsMacUtilsImpl::GetAppPath already does for the sandbox's APP_PATH) keeps
every child off the link without widening any sandbox.

diff --git a/ipc/glue/GeckoChildProcessHost.cpp b/ipc/glue/GeckoChildProcessHost.cpp
index 4ce81491b7..075f1ca913 100644
--- a/ipc/glue/GeckoChildProcessHost.cpp
+++ b/ipc/glue/GeckoChildProcessHost.cpp
@@ -564,6 +564,12 @@ mozilla::BinPathType BaseProcessLauncher::GetPathToBinary(
     nsCOMPtr<nsIFile> childProcPath;
     if (NS_SUCCEEDED(NS_NewLocalFile(nsDependentString(gGREBinPath),
                                      getter_AddRefs(childProcPath)))) {
+      // Launch the child by its real path. A sandboxed child resolves every
+      // path it derives from its executable, and resolving one through a
+      // symlink needs file-read-metadata on the link, which
+      // SandboxPolicyUtility does not grant: launched through a link, a
+      // utility process never connects.
+      (void)childProcPath->Normalize();
